### Phase 4: Keycloak endpoints (VS Code "REST Client" extension).
### The Authorization Code + PKCE login needs a browser-style form post; use
###   ./infrastructure/keycloak/pkce-login.sh alice
### and paste the printed access token into @accessToken below.

@kc = http://localhost:8180
@realm = {{kc}}/realms/banking
@oidc = {{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect
@accessToken = paste-access-token-here
@refreshToken = paste-refresh-token-here
@paymentSecret = paste-PAYMENT_SERVICE_CLIENT_SECRET-from-.env

### OIDC discovery: everything a client needs to know about this Identity Provider
GET {{realm}}/.well-known/openid-configuration

### JWKS: public keys used to verify token signatures (fetched by gateway and services)
GET {{oidc}}/certs

### UserInfo: profile claims for the token's user (requires scope openid)
GET {{oidc}}/userinfo
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Refresh: new access token + new refresh token (the old one is now invalid: rotation)
POST {{oidc}}/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=refresh_token&client_id=banking-frontend&refresh_token={{refreshToken}}

### Logout: ends the SSO session (all refresh tokens of that session stop working)
POST {{oidc}}/logout
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=banking-frontend&refresh_token={{refreshToken}}

### Client Credentials: payment-service gets a token AS ITSELF (no user involved)
# @name serviceToken
POST {{oidc}}/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=payment-service&client_secret={{paymentSecret}}

### Password grant: deliberately disabled (expect unauthorized_client)
POST {{oidc}}/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=banking-frontend&username=alice&password=whatever
